(7453344, 1180181, 114285, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the PB, you''re rocking it lately, this is one of the nicest photo''s I''ve seen on here with a landscape/person in it for a long time, you sure do live in a gorgeous part of SA, I hope your grand daughter gets a copy to put on her wall, adding as a fave!</td>', 'Congrats on the PB, you''re rocking it lately, this is one of the nicest photo''s I''ve seen on here with a landscape/person in it for a long time, you sure do live in a gorgeous part of SA, I hope your grand daughter gets a copy to put on her wall, adding as a fave!', '2016-05-04 01:05:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(7453345, 1180181, 104230, '<td valign="top">Great image for a new PB.  Congratulations.  So glad you came back after taking a break from DPC! Love how you captured the dew on the grasses.  Great contrast to the misty softness.</td>', 'Great image for a new PB.  Congratulations.  So glad you came back after taking a break from DPC! Love how you captured the dew on the grasses.  Great contrast to the misty softness.', '2016-05-04 01:08:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7453348, 1180198, 136989, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First things first ...  Definitely an intense portrait. A good fit for the quote selected and the challenge. Nothing conjures music like a guitar.  I love the drama created by the single eye stare and the balance between black and white created by hat, shirt and instrument.  Sitting here wishing I could hear the melody ...<br/> <br/>From a detail/clarity perspective ... Nice work on catching the details where it matters most (face and instrument to fit the quote) while allowing the rest to fade a bit into the background.  This offsets the intensity nicely with a little hint at the um ... Heat that created that fire.  Please play on....<br/> <br/>~Cia</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First things first ...  Definitely an intense portrait. A good fit for the quote selected and the challenge. Nothing conjures music like a guitar.  I love the drama created by the single eye stare and the balance between black and white created by hat, shirt and instrument.  Sitting here wishing I could hear the melody ... From a detail/clarity perspective ... Nice work on catching the details where it matters most (face and instrument to fit the quote) while allowing the rest to fade a bit into the background.  This offsets the intensity nicely with a little hint at the um ... Heat that created that fire.  Please play on.... ~Cia', '2016-05-04 01:40:47.000000', NULL, 0),
